    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nExecuting `lua print()` in the headless child process doesn't print to the command line after 58ce7218ec9a (#42064).\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create the following `init.lua`:\n\n    ```lua\n    _G.new_child = function()\n      -- Start\n      local child = { address = vim.fn.tempname() }\n      local args = { vim.v.progpath, '--clean', '-n', '--listen', child.address, '--headless' }\n      child.id = vim.fn.jobstart(args)\n\n      -- Attach after making sure that the process is created\n      vim.uv.sleep(500)\n      child.channel = vim.fn.sockconnect('pipe', child.address, { rpc = true })\n\n      -- Helper to capture the output of `:lua print()`\n      child.cmd_capture = function(cmd) return vim.rpcrequest(child.channel, 'nvim_exec2', cmd, { output = true }) end\n\n      -- Helper to print into the command line\n      child.cmd = function(cmd) return vim.rpcrequest(child.channel, 'nvim_exec2', cmd, {}) end\n\n      child.get_screenshot = function()\n        return vim.rpcrequest(child.channel, 'nvim_exec_lua', [[\n          local text = {}\n          for i = 1, vim.o.lines do\n            local text_line = {}\n            for j = 1, vim.o.columns do\n              table.insert(text_line, vim.fn.screenstring(i, j))\n            end\n            table.insert(text, table.concat(text_line))\n          end\n          return text\n        ]], {})\n      end\n\n      return child\n    end\n    ```\n\n2. `nvim --clean -u init.lua`\n3. `:lua child = new_child()`\n4. Do one of the following:\n    4.1 `:=child.cmd_capture('lua print(\"Hello\")')`. This prints `{ output = \"\" }` when before #42064 it printed `{ output = \"Hello\" }`.\n    4.2 `:lua child.cmd('lua print(\"World\")')` followed by `:=child.get_screenshot()`. The last line doesn't contain `World`, when before #42064 it did. The `child.cmd('echo \"World\"')` works as expected, though.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nExecuting `:lua print()` in the active child Neovim process prints to the instance's command line.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1793+g1dc9728dbd\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS Linux x86_64, 7.2.7-arch1-1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nAppimage and from source",
